mental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 5%.","Capex runs 1.7x depreciation (6.9% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 24, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.5%, and institutions hold 80%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (9 sales, net $5.7M sold).","Short interest is elevated at 14.9% of the float, 1.6 days to cover."],"people":["With about 141,100 employees, each generates about $387K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 6.2% a year across its filed history.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$5K per employee.","CEO pay is $1.4M (4x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":null,"vc":null,"med":{"pe":22.1377,"ev_ebitda":12.904,"pfcf":21.8001,"pb":2.7623,"roic":0.0997,"gross_margin":0.2864,"fcf_margin":0.0677,"div_yield":0.0151}},"ticker":"AAL","date":"2026-11-20"}